vLLM PR #60045 "[Bugfix][Core] Count only held blocks against the sliding window admission cap", head commit 843db1462a066076d407bb628098140da4455be5 (open, not merged; https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60045), core change only, backported to vLLM 0.31.0.
Layby Phase R: every vLLM arm (stock baselines and Layby alike) runs with it. Stock 0.31.0 caps a sliding-window group's
admission count at max_admission_blocks_per_request, then subtracts the null-padded positions below the window, so a
request with a long prefix hit counts 0 window blocks in the full-sequence check and in the in-flight reservation
(Scheduler._request_remaining_blocks). Two async loads admitted together on Gemma 4 31B held 2 x 1,006 of 2,188 blocks
and neither could take its next chunk. The PR counts the live blocks from the window's first block, capped, minus the
real blocks held or hit. Per-step allocation is unchanged.
Stock file sha256 3a3cb20bd6aa1e0ad46471fc9e5e01ee5797ab4bb759e00ef5fb309d2830db13 (vllm 0.31.0 wheel).
Apply: PYTHON engine/phase_r/vllm/apply_patch.py apply (the python of the environment that runs vLLM).

